WEBVTT


00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.499
<i>This has been America News
Radio from Washington.</i>


00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:14.138
<i>Now back to your local
ANR station for news on the hour.</i>


00:02:15.098 --> 00:02:21.016
<i>Good evening. You're listening
to 108.9 FM, KMZR, Portland. This...</i>


00:02:37.049 --> 00:02:38.169
Evening, ma'am.


00:03:36.627 --> 00:03:38.266
You, too.


00:03:47.263 --> 00:03:48.702
- Good evening.
- Good evening.


00:03:48.863 --> 00:03:51.222
- Careful. Careful, it's hot.
- Thank you.


00:03:51.382 --> 00:03:54.541
- Busy night for the bad guys?
- Even busier night for us.


00:04:00.858 --> 00:04:02.977
Okay.


00:04:03.257 --> 00:04:05.296
Let's see what you got for me.


00:04:09.855 --> 00:04:12.693
Oh, hey,
because you're dying to know...


00:04:12.854 --> 00:04:16.812
...l'm almost positive my first date last
night is eligible for the hall of fame.


00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.811
She was amazing.
She looked exactly like her photo.


00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.410
You'll never see her again.


00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.569
- How do you know?
- Because you look nothing like yours.


00:04:27.808 --> 00:04:29.447
Nice one.


00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:48.640
- Here's that guy I was telling you about.
- Oh, yeah?


00:04:48.841 --> 00:04:51.759
He changes his name every day.
It's taken me a week to isolate him.


00:04:51.919 --> 00:04:53.479
Listen to this.


00:04:54.598 --> 00:04:57.277
- Tunethief.com.
- Oh, how original.


00:04:57.916 --> 00:05:00.003
Yeah, he offers free downloads
of pirated music.


00:05:00.196 --> 00:05:02.276
I'm running this
in a fake virtual machine.


00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:04.634
Watch what happens
when I accept his offer.


00:05:05.754 --> 00:05:08.153
Now, he's stealing my financial data...


00:05:08.433 --> 00:05:10.192
...and all my passwords.


00:05:10.872 --> 00:05:13.631
Which I happened to have gathered
in a file called "passwords."


00:05:13.791 --> 00:05:15.510
Nice touch.


00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.069
I threw in a backdoor Trojan so
we can see what he's doing with it.


00:05:19.229 --> 00:05:22.268
He's run up a quarter-million dollars
in fraud the past three weeks.


00:05:22.428 --> 00:05:25.587
- Well, what's he into?
- High-end tech and low-end porn.


00:05:25.786 --> 00:05:29.865
God. You sure it's a guy? If it's
a woman, she could be my soul mate.


00:05:30.025 --> 00:05:31.384
Send it over to me.


00:05:32.664 --> 00:05:34.383
There you go.


00:05:34.783 --> 00:05:36.943
My dummy Capital One card.
Hope he goes for it.


00:05:37.142 --> 00:05:38.221
Okay, I see it.


00:05:40.581 --> 00:05:43.260
I'm surprised he has
the patience for auctions.


00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.379
- Oh, you've got him now.
- Okay, there's his IP address.


00:05:47.858 --> 00:05:49.378
Let's get his physical one.


00:05:49.538 --> 00:05:52.616
Portland Police sent this over.
They weren't sure what to do with it.


00:05:52.776 --> 00:05:54.216
Thank you.


00:05:55.375 --> 00:05:57.734
- It is a woman.
- ER nurse, lives alone.


00:05:59.054 --> 00:06:01.253
No priors,
no history of online purchases.


00:06:01.413 --> 00:06:03.052
It's not her. Gotta be a neighbor...


00:06:03.212 --> 00:06:06.731
...somebody close by, someone
who could access her wireless router.


00:06:06.891 --> 00:06:09.770
Sharon Dobbs lives here.


00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.929
All right. Here we go,
here's somebody.


00:06:14.488 --> 00:06:18.087
Sam Barrows. He's a computer
programmer for the school district.


00:06:18.246 --> 00:06:20.086
He's lived there six weeks.
He's a renter.


00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:23.125
He's registered for three handguns
and two assault rifles.


00:06:23.285 --> 00:06:24.284
That's your guy.


00:06:24.444 --> 00:06:27.244
Jennifer Marsh, FBI Cyber Crimes
up in Portland.


00:06:27.404 --> 00:06:29.563
We need you to knock down
a door for us.


00:06:46.077 --> 00:06:48.595
Oh, I gotta get reassigned.


00:06:48.956 --> 00:06:50.555
What's the matter?


00:06:50.715 --> 00:06:52.954
It's just a sickness. It's just too much.


00:06:53.114 --> 00:06:55.153
I got this
retired high school principal...


00:06:55.353 --> 00:06:57.527
...offering to come over
to where I'm babysitting.


00:06:57.672 --> 00:07:00.192
He's got so many chats,
he can't keep his names straight.


00:07:00.351 --> 00:07:02.471
He keeps calling me Jill
instead of Molly.


00:07:02.631 --> 00:07:05.549
I'm only interested in what his
cellmates are gonna call him.


00:07:05.749 --> 00:07:07.468
I'm taking a break. Do you want?


00:07:07.628 --> 00:07:09.988
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.020
All right.


00:07:44.415 --> 00:07:47.933
I see feet! Get your hands up!
Get your hands up!


00:07:48.093 --> 00:07:50.653
On your stomach! On your stomach!


00:08:07.046 --> 00:08:09.045
<i>- on flawless, cut Natalie K
diamonds.</i>


00:08:09.246 --> 00:08:13.204
<i>Huge savings on one-karat diamonds.
Presented by the LaRog Brothers.</i>


00:08:17.043 --> 00:08:19.869
- What the hell is this?
- I don't know. I'm running it down now.


00:08:19.962 --> 00:08:21.201
It is streaming live.


00:08:21.401 --> 00:08:23.760
Just when you thought
you've seen it all.


00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.519
Oh, look, a message from our sponsor.


00:08:26.679 --> 00:08:29.558
"Ha-ha. Only serious."


00:08:32.437 --> 00:08:33.716
Jennifer Marsh, Cyber Crimes.


00:08:34.117 --> 00:08:37.315
Carter Thompson here.
I'm at the Barrow residence.


00:08:37.755 --> 00:08:40.674
The suspect's in custody.
Hard drive's intact.


00:08:40.834 --> 00:08:44.712
<i>- Plenty of contraband.
- Good work. Hey, let me guess.</i>


00:08:44.872 --> 00:08:47.991
It's not just Barrow. His son's
involved. He's got a son?


00:08:48.151 --> 00:08:49.551
<i>What makes you say that?</i>


00:08:49.711 --> 00:08:52.030
Well, high-tech toys and porn...


00:08:52.229 --> 00:08:54.828
...and then out of the blue,
he buys a gold wristwatch.


00:08:54.988 --> 00:08:56.868
How come? And then it hit me.


00:08:57.027 --> 00:09:01.387
01-10-57.
Sunday's his father's birthday.


00:09:02.626 --> 00:09:04.385
Sweet dreams, Marsh.


00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:11.142
<i>Good morning.</i>


00:09:11.302 --> 00:09:14.661
<i>We'll return to America News Radio
after the local news and weather.</i>


00:09:14.822 --> 00:09:16.500
<i>It's the 7:00 hour.</i>


00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:20.180
<i>This is KMZR, 108.9 FM, Portland.</i>


00:09:20.339 --> 00:09:24.378
<i>And on the Web at mzrnews.org.
First, the weather.</i>


00:09:24.379 --> 00:09:28.055
<i>The hurricane system that has poured
3 inches of rain on western Portland...</i>


00:09:28.056 --> 00:09:30.815
<i>... in the past 24 hours
has finally let up.</i>


00:09:30.975 --> 00:09:34.453
<i>Though there is no sign of an easing
of the near-freezing temperatures...</i>


00:09:35.934 --> 00:09:40.052
<i>OnStar operator Tina. Good morning,
Ms. Marsh. How can I assist you?</i>


00:09:40.211 --> 00:09:42.011
Yes, Tina.


00:09:42.411 --> 00:09:45.729
I'd like to get home
sometime before Easter.


00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:47.649
I'm in a traffic jam here.


00:09:47.809 --> 00:09:49.768
<i>Okay, let's see.</i>


00:09:49.929 --> 00:09:52.727
<i>You're in the middle
of a gaper's block.</i>


00:09:52.887 --> 00:09:56.565
<i>You should be past the accident
in about 100 yards.</i>


00:09:56.726 --> 00:10:01.404
<i>- Okay, I see it now. Thank you.
- You're welcome.</i>


00:10:04.482 --> 00:10:07.082
Come on, keep it moving.


00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.909
- Shit, you scared me.
- Watch your mouth, young lady.


00:10:42.389 --> 00:10:46.307
Hey, that's what I said to you
when you were a kid.


00:10:46.467 --> 00:10:49.546
I know, Mom. That's what
makes it so darn funny.


00:10:49.706 --> 00:10:51.385
Oh, somebody's crabby.


00:10:51.545 --> 00:10:54.304
Sorry. Long night.


00:11:09.179 --> 00:11:11.018
Mom!


00:11:11.178 --> 00:11:13.737
- Look at the outfit I'm making.
- I can see that.


00:11:13.897 --> 00:11:16.616
- You're stealing my job.
- You were late.


00:11:16.776 --> 00:11:19.975
I know. I'm sorry about that, sweetie.


00:11:20.854 --> 00:11:22.054
Catch any bad guys?


00:11:23.373 --> 00:11:26.013
One. Just one.


00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:32.450
Okay, I'm coming.


00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:36.569
Slowpoke. The slowest poke
I've ever seen, ever.


00:11:37.328 --> 00:11:39.127
I'm coming.


00:11:41.767 --> 00:11:44.165
- How are things with you and Maddy?
- Better.


00:11:44.366 --> 00:11:46.845
Mrs. Tischler's gonna
give us a second chance.


00:11:47.005 --> 00:11:50.284
- A second chance at what?
- Being friends.


00:11:50.444 --> 00:11:53.122
Oh, of course. I think that's great.


00:11:53.442 --> 00:11:56.641
She can come to my party now.
Make sure to send her mom an Evite.


00:11:56.801 --> 00:11:58.681
- You got it.
- Maybe Grandma should do it.


00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:00.101
- I'll do it.
- Are you sure?


00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:03.159
When I say I'll do it, I'll do it,
okay? I promise.


00:12:03.319 --> 00:12:05.398
- I love you.
- I love you, too, babe.


00:12:13.315 --> 00:12:16.634
I bet you'd like me
to do this some other time!


00:12:42.264 --> 00:12:44.184
Hey, friendly.


00:13:34.085 --> 00:13:37.084
All right, Jennifer. Let's see
this tortured kitty of yours.


00:13:37.244 --> 00:13:39.083
Torture's over, sir.


00:13:39.723 --> 00:13:43.041
- Yeah, I should say so.
- Poor Lulu.


00:13:43.201 --> 00:13:44.601
That was the cat's name.


00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:48.040
The owner, Scotty Hillman,
26, from West Linn...


00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:52.118
...says she was snatched a few days
ago from his lawn during a yard sale.


00:13:52.318 --> 00:13:54.157
He recognized her fancy collar.


00:13:54.317 --> 00:13:55.837
West Linn. So this site...


00:13:55.997 --> 00:13:58.796
...which could have originated
anywhere from Oslo to Istanbul...


00:13:58.955 --> 00:14:00.475
Is local. Yes, sir.


00:14:00.635 --> 00:14:02.194
The odds of that are pretty steep.


00:14:02.394 --> 00:14:05.473
About a million to one, if it were
a coincidence, which it's not.


00:14:05.633 --> 00:14:08.632
The only way we found out about this
is because it was tipped...


00:14:08.792 --> 00:14:12.670
...to the county sheriff's office and the
police within minutes of it going up.


00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:15.669
Both tips came from a pay phone
in the central city...


00:14:15.829 --> 00:14:19.308
...so whoever is behind the site
is local and wants attention.


00:14:19.468 --> 00:14:21.347
- Shut him down.
- I just did.


00:14:24.466 --> 00:14:26.825
- There you go.
- I'll type the address in again.


00:14:33.902 --> 00:14:35.462
It's been doing that all night.


00:14:35.622 --> 00:14:39.381
The site's IP changes constantly. Each
new address is an exploited server...


00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:41.339
...that's running a mirror of the site.


00:14:41.739 --> 00:14:44.259
The site's Russian name server
uses a low TTL...


00:14:44.459 --> 00:14:47.338
...so your computer constantly queries
the name server's record.


00:14:47.497 --> 00:14:49.737
That's how it gives
you a new address consistently.


00:14:49.897 --> 00:14:52.496
There are thousands of exploited
servers on the Internet...


00:14:52.656 --> 00:14:54.655
...so he won't run out of victims soon.


00:14:54.815 --> 00:14:56.694
He's accessing these machines
so quickly...


00:14:56.854 --> 00:14:58.973
...he's got to be
running his own botnet.


00:14:59.173 --> 00:15:00.573
We are blackholing these IPs...


00:15:00.773 --> 00:15:03.731
...but every time we shut one down,
a new mirror pops up.


00:15:03.892 --> 00:15:06.170
I don't understand a single word
you just said.


00:15:06.371 --> 00:15:08.049
What does Russia
have to do with this?


00:15:08.209 --> 00:15:11.248
The domain registrar
and name servers are all in Russia.


00:15:11.409 --> 00:15:13.328
We have no jurisdiction there.


00:15:13.928 --> 00:15:15.726
Jennifer...


00:15:15.887 --> 00:15:17.566
...it's a cat.
- Yeah.


00:15:17.726 --> 00:15:20.965
Considering the state of the world,
aren't there more important things...


00:15:21.125 --> 00:15:24.444
...to be concerned about, like
something under our jurisdiction?


00:15:26.923 --> 00:15:28.962
Back to work, gentlemen.


00:15:38.958 --> 00:15:42.480
<i>Things are about to get warmer when
one of the hottest hockey rivalries...</i>


00:16:16.264 --> 00:16:19.263
Are you the guy? You got the
extra ticket for the hockey game?


00:16:40.176 --> 00:16:43.934
Grandma! Grandma! Grandma!


00:16:44.094 --> 00:16:45.573
- Did you get it?
- Yes, I did!


00:16:45.733 --> 00:16:47.693
Oh, my God, I'm so proud of you!


00:16:47.853 --> 00:16:50.651
And the boy I fought was so tall too.


00:16:50.812 --> 00:16:53.930
- Careful, I'm all wet.
- So am I.


00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:57.170
We celebrated. We had an ice cream.


00:16:57.649 --> 00:16:59.209
Hello.


00:17:35.755 --> 00:17:36.754
Mom?


00:17:36.915 --> 00:17:39.114
- Honey... Mom, please!
- Okay, okay.


00:17:39.274 --> 00:17:41.472
Come on, baby.
Let's get you out of these clothes.


00:17:45.951 --> 00:17:49.470
I've been monitoring the site all week.
Nothing but a still of the dead kitten.


00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:52.509
Last night around 11, the site
went down, I'd hoped forever.


00:17:52.709 --> 00:17:57.027
Anyway, a few minutes ago, this.


00:17:58.747 --> 00:18:01.186
It's the same basement
still streaming live.


00:18:01.346 --> 00:18:05.224
The top is the number of active viewers
and some chemical-dosage flow.


00:18:05.384 --> 00:18:07.983
He's carved the name of the website
into the guy's chest.


00:18:08.143 --> 00:18:09.662
He's threatening to drain him.


00:18:09.822 --> 00:18:12.781
Threatening to drain what, his blood?
How's he gonna do that?


00:18:12.941 --> 00:18:15.540
Those letters aren't any deeper
than paper cuts.


00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:17.100
Not the cuts, it's the bleeding.


00:18:17.259 --> 00:18:20.138
We think that box regulates
the fluid going into the victim.


00:18:20.298 --> 00:18:23.017
Those cables are probably
connected to our guy's computer.


00:18:23.177 --> 00:18:25.776
Look, his nose is starting
to bleed and he's bruising.


00:18:25.936 --> 00:18:28.335
We think those bags have
some anticoagulant in them.


00:18:28.535 --> 00:18:31.574
I've got a list of them right here.
The most common is heparin.


00:18:31.734 --> 00:18:35.733
If you get the dose right, you save a
life. Wrong, you've got a hemophiliac.


00:18:36.652 --> 00:18:39.851
So the more people who visit the site,
the more the drug is released...


00:18:40.051 --> 00:18:41.290
...and the faster he bleeds.


00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:43.850
- That's what we believe.
- Well, isn't that wonderful?


00:18:44.049 --> 00:18:47.408
Well, if that counter is accurate,
the public would seem to agree.


00:18:47.568 --> 00:18:49.448
They're tuning in at an alarming rate.


00:18:49.608 --> 00:18:51.807
The victim's name
is Herbert Miller, 54.


00:18:51.966 --> 00:18:55.205
Lives in Sellwood, works
for Burnside Executive Charter.


00:18:55.366 --> 00:18:59.124
Friday night, got back from a shuttle
to Mount Hood, called his wife...


00:18:59.284 --> 00:19:02.402
...says that he gets an e-mail
from a friend of a friend...


00:19:02.603 --> 00:19:05.321
...offering center-ice seats
to the Winter Hawks game.


00:19:05.482 --> 00:19:07.440
He promises
he'll be home afterwards.


00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.400
- He wasn't.
- Any priors?


00:19:10.519 --> 00:19:12.919
- Who, Miller?
- Why is that relevant?


00:19:13.118 --> 00:19:15.717
Remember that snuff film
sent to the L.A. office last year?


00:19:15.878 --> 00:19:18.637
Teenage geisha cut in two.
Looked as real as anything you saw.


00:19:18.797 --> 00:19:22.515
Six weeks later, they found her alive
and well, waiting tables in Little Tokyo.


00:19:22.675 --> 00:19:25.434
Maybe Miller's involved somehow.
Maybe there's a connection.


00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:39.668
What are you doing to me?


00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.259
Mrs. Miller!


00:20:09.297 --> 00:20:10.897
Just go away. Just leave.


00:20:11.057 --> 00:20:13.816
- Okay, folks, one side, please.
- I don't know.


00:20:13.976 --> 00:20:16.615
Come on. Police.
Coming through. Mrs. Miller.


00:20:17.135 --> 00:20:19.054
Back off. Back off. Mrs. Miller.


00:20:19.214 --> 00:20:21.779
- Portland Police. May we come in?
- Thank God you're here.


00:20:21.933 --> 00:20:23.972
I need you to back off right now.


00:20:25.651 --> 00:20:29.330
My name is Detective Box.
This is my partner, Detective Moy.


00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:33.288
Listen, is there someplace
else we can talk?


00:20:34.248 --> 00:20:35.488
Yeah, let's go outside.


00:20:42.566 --> 00:20:45.244
Oh, shit. Fuck!


00:20:46.404 --> 00:20:49.361
<i>So, Mrs. Miller, when was the
last time you saw your husband?</i>


00:20:50.083 --> 00:20:51.482
Yesterday morning.


00:20:51.682 --> 00:20:56.880
He called, and he said he'd got tickets
to the Winter Hawks game last night.


00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:00.799
He likes hockey, and I just wanted
him to come straight home.


00:21:00.959 --> 00:21:02.998
Okay. Listen...


00:21:03.197 --> 00:21:06.596
...I understand what you're going
through is very difficult. All right?


00:21:06.756 --> 00:21:10.434
But you're making it worse by talking
to the press. Don't talk to the press.


00:21:10.595 --> 00:21:11.795
Do you understand? Listen.


00:21:11.954 --> 00:21:15.473
Don't talk to the press
and stay off the computer. Okay?


00:21:36.585 --> 00:21:39.504
Listen to this. I'm running the logs
from that mirror we took down.


00:21:39.664 --> 00:21:43.743
He's blocking all the foreign IPs. Only
Americans can gain access to the site.


00:21:43.902 --> 00:21:45.821
How patriotic.


00:21:46.381 --> 00:21:49.461
We've scanned every newsgroup,
chat room, blog, website and forum...


00:21:49.621 --> 00:21:53.059
...referencing "Kill With Me,"
and I think we found our first post.


00:21:53.259 --> 00:21:56.738
It appeared just before the site went
up, then it was spammed Web-wide.


00:21:56.898 --> 00:21:59.337
"A cat caught in a rattrap.
How's that for irony?


00:21:59.497 --> 00:22:02.455
It's streaming live on killwithme.com.
It's awesome. Check it out."


00:22:02.616 --> 00:22:05.334
It was posted by a sophomore
named Andrew Kilburn.


00:22:05.494 --> 00:22:09.373
It came from his account, but it didn't
actually originate from his computer.


00:22:09.532 --> 00:22:12.332
So our guy hacked his account
and used it to start the thread.


00:22:12.492 --> 00:22:14.611
- Yeah.
- Let's go after the originating IP.


00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:20.289
Oh, God.


00:22:20.449 --> 00:22:22.248
It's too bad this guy wasn't
a Boy Scout.


00:22:22.409 --> 00:22:24.847
He could just blink Morse code
and tell us where he is.


00:22:38.122 --> 00:22:42.121
Okay, I've got the "who is."
It comes back Blue Sky ISP.


00:22:42.281 --> 00:22:46.120
- Username and password, please.
- Coming to you now.


00:22:49.078 --> 00:22:51.637
- "Chang's Restaurant"?
- He hacked into their site?


00:22:51.797 --> 00:22:54.476
No. No. Half the office eats there.


00:22:54.676 --> 00:22:57.515
He's messing with us.
He wanted us to find this.


00:22:57.675 --> 00:22:59.714
Who the hell is this guy?


00:23:06.392 --> 00:23:08.791
Jennifer Marsh, Detective Eric Box.


00:23:08.951 --> 00:23:11.070
Portland Police has him
on the Miller abduction.


00:23:11.229 --> 00:23:14.469
- Jennifer's our case agent on this.
- Case agent, sir?


00:23:14.629 --> 00:23:16.388
- You caught it, you got it.
- Please.


00:23:16.588 --> 00:23:19.387
Sir, anyone else. You know I'm
on nights because of my daughter.


00:23:19.547 --> 00:23:21.386
I understand that, but you're it.


00:23:22.666 --> 00:23:24.385
- We forming a task force?
- Not yet.


00:23:24.585 --> 00:23:26.305
Not yet?
How much more do you need?


00:23:26.504 --> 00:23:29.983
So far we have one dead cat and a man
who may or may not be in danger...


00:23:30.183 --> 00:23:33.342
That's today. You think this is it?
It's just the beginning.


00:23:33.861 --> 00:23:35.301
Marsh, hold it.


00:23:35.461 --> 00:23:38.099
You share what you've got,
and then you take it from there.


00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:40.819
Appreciate your coming in, detective.


00:23:43.698 --> 00:23:45.857
All right. You first.


00:23:46.257 --> 00:23:49.056
Well, we found Miller's car
in the Rose Garden parking lot.


00:23:49.215 --> 00:23:51.055
No prints but his own.


00:23:51.215 --> 00:23:54.014
We passed out photos of the
basement to some local contractors.


00:23:54.174 --> 00:23:57.493
They say, judging from the timbers,
the house was built in the '20s or '30s.


00:23:57.693 --> 00:24:00.692
Which narrows it down to,
you know, half the city.


00:24:03.731 --> 00:24:04.690
Yeah, what else?


00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:07.489
Miller appears to be a decent guy.
He's a Vietnam vet...


00:24:07.649 --> 00:24:10.528
...coaches his daughter's soccer,
they go to church every Sunday.


00:24:10.688 --> 00:24:12.727
So why'd the subject pick him?


00:24:13.567 --> 00:24:15.086
"Subject"?


00:24:15.966 --> 00:24:17.365
Are we in science class?


00:24:18.085 --> 00:24:20.684
- What would you prefer?
- How about "piece of shit"?


00:24:22.204 --> 00:24:23.643
Why Miller?


00:24:24.243 --> 00:24:26.442
I don't know. Maybe it was random.


00:24:26.602 --> 00:24:28.361
What about the kitten?
Talk to that guy?


00:24:28.521 --> 00:24:30.640
Scotty Hillman, yeah.
He's a fucking jackass.


00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:33.119
All he cares about is getting
the kitten's collar...


00:24:33.279 --> 00:24:36.079
...because he paid 12 bucks
for it on bidityours.com


00:24:36.238 --> 00:24:38.958
Which I suppose is a lot of money
if you're flipping burgers.


00:24:39.117 --> 00:24:42.436
What I would like to know is,
why him? Why his kitten?


00:24:42.636 --> 00:24:45.834
Why take the risk of stealing when
you can get one free at any shelter?


00:24:46.315 --> 00:24:48.954
- What do you guys got?
- It's a website.


00:24:49.114 --> 00:24:52.072
It's like nothing we've ever seen.
It's extremely sophisticated.


00:24:52.233 --> 00:24:55.231
As long as its source-streaming site
is a ghost, it's untraceable.


00:24:56.111 --> 00:24:59.070
This guy can invite the world to help
him kill Miller or anybody...


00:24:59.230 --> 00:25:01.949
...and there's not a goddamn thing
we can do about it.


00:25:06.387 --> 00:25:07.906
Excuse me.


00:25:16.944 --> 00:25:20.142
- It's over.
- Yeah.


00:25:20.702 --> 00:25:24.341
The numbers, they just... exploded.


00:25:30.458 --> 00:25:33.017
"Rolling on the floor laughing.


00:25:33.177 --> 00:25:34.297
Thank you for..."


00:25:35.136 --> 00:25:37.496
"For all your support.


00:25:37.656 --> 00:25:38.855
More to come."


00:25:41.014 --> 00:25:43.053
Well, we'll see about that.


00:25:46.892 --> 00:25:49.011
It's a jungle in there.


00:26:17.001 --> 00:26:21.039
<i>Hey, I just went to the site
after the guy was dead...</i>


00:26:21.040 --> 00:26:24.677
<i>I got a list of assholes my girlfriends
and me think he ought to kill next.</i>


00:26:24.678 --> 00:26:30.556
<i>Last seen five days ago, FBI agents
have been working around the clock...</i>


00:26:39.912 --> 00:26:41.512
There's a pickup truck.


00:26:41.672 --> 00:26:43.551
What's that on the back, a gun rack?


00:26:43.871 --> 00:26:47.550
Yeah, well, there's no way that freak is
stepping foot in my dad's country club.


00:26:47.710 --> 00:26:49.469
So call Tucker.


00:27:03.144 --> 00:27:05.862
<i>- at 7: 15 a.m., a vehicle at the
home...</i>


00:27:06.022 --> 00:27:08.621
<i>... of Oregon congressman
Joseph A. Restom.</i>


00:27:08.822 --> 00:27:11.661
<i>Herbert Miller had been the focus
of an intense local...</i>


00:27:11.662 --> 00:27:13.899
<i>... and statewide police
and FBI search...</i>


00:27:13.900 --> 00:27:16.204
<i>... since midday Saturday
when he showed up...</i>


00:27:16.339 --> 00:27:19.938
...on an Internet website
being tortured and murdered live.


00:27:20.097 --> 00:27:23.616
Now, because of the uniqueness
of the crime, and because the FBI...


00:27:23.776 --> 00:27:27.455
...is able to provide resources
critical to this investigation...


00:27:28.054 --> 00:27:32.012
...they will be leading the interagency
task force assigned to the case.


00:27:32.972 --> 00:27:36.931
He flew helicopters for a living. What's
his connection to a U.S. congressman?


00:27:37.091 --> 00:27:40.649
Our guy had to dump the body.
Why not on a national stage?


00:27:40.809 --> 00:27:43.968
You think he did it to get a press
conference? Build up his fan base?


00:27:44.169 --> 00:27:46.048
Don't call them fans.
They're accomplices.


00:27:46.248 --> 00:27:49.007
All right, whatever.
Why'd he choose Restom?


00:27:49.166 --> 00:27:50.446
He's owned by Silicon Valley.


00:27:50.606 --> 00:27:53.445
He sits on the House Judiciary
Committee on Net neutrality.


00:27:53.605 --> 00:27:56.283
No restriction on content,
all traffic treated equally.


00:27:56.484 --> 00:27:59.162
- Wouldn't our guy be for that?
- You'd think so.


00:27:59.322 --> 00:28:01.202
Miller's clients
were corporate executives.


00:28:01.362 --> 00:28:02.761
Maybe some were from high-tech.


00:28:02.921 --> 00:28:04.841
I'll track down a customer list.


00:28:05.001 --> 00:28:07.839
- What about the neighbors?
- One saw a van drive by at 4 a.m.


00:28:07.999 --> 00:28:09.998
Another heard a car door slam
a minute later.


00:28:10.158 --> 00:28:12.078
Figured it was the paper
being delivered.


00:28:12.238 --> 00:28:14.277
Excuse me a second.
Might have something here.


00:28:14.437 --> 00:28:16.756
- What is it?
- Tip just came in through a hot line.


00:28:16.916 --> 00:28:21.114
Guy named Arthur James Elmer, an
engineer at Chadwick Technologies.


00:28:21.274 --> 00:28:23.313
He was fired six months ago...


00:28:23.514 --> 00:28:25.873
...for installing a wireless Webcam
in the men's room.


00:28:26.032 --> 00:28:29.231
Nice. Anyway, he's been talking
about killwithme.com nonstop...


00:28:29.392 --> 00:28:31.550
...ever since the kitty died.
Wanna ride with us?


00:28:31.711 --> 00:28:33.550
Let me check this guy out
on my end.


00:28:33.710 --> 00:28:35.749
- We'll catch up later.
- Yeah.


00:29:03.338 --> 00:29:06.538
- So, what's going on?
- He won't let us in. Kind of shy.


00:29:13.775 --> 00:29:15.255
Elmer.


00:29:17.694 --> 00:29:21.013
Look, if you didn't do anything,
you got nothing to lose letting us in.


00:29:21.972 --> 00:29:25.331
And if you did, we can always
come back with a warrant.


00:29:28.009 --> 00:29:30.049
So how do you wanna play it?


00:29:38.006 --> 00:29:39.445
Hi.


00:29:40.405 --> 00:29:41.925
I'm Detective Box.


00:29:42.085 --> 00:29:44.244
Unusual name.


00:29:45.563 --> 00:29:47.603
Well, it wasn't up to me.


00:29:49.841 --> 00:29:53.280
So you really think I killed that guy?


00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:56.639
I don't know. Did you?


00:29:57.599 --> 00:29:58.878
Well, I'm flattered.


00:29:59.038 --> 00:30:02.077
I found it highly entertaining,
especially at the end.


00:30:02.237 --> 00:30:04.236
The way viewership
increased exponentially...


00:30:04.396 --> 00:30:07.435
...like some sort of epidemic.


00:30:08.395 --> 00:30:10.154
Can I see the basement?


00:30:50.819 --> 00:30:52.498
You like movies, huh?


00:30:53.378 --> 00:30:54.817
Yeah, who doesn't?


00:30:56.097 --> 00:30:57.497
Me.


00:30:59.935 --> 00:31:01.615
Burn your own copies?


00:31:01.775 --> 00:31:03.214
You know that's illegal, right?


00:31:14.131 --> 00:31:16.249
Can't say they didn't warn you.


00:31:30.884 --> 00:31:33.363
Got our proof it wasn't Elmer.


00:31:34.162 --> 00:31:35.762
Starting Friday at 1 p. m...


00:31:36.082 --> 00:31:39.960
...Elmer was logged into a chat
room for 12 consecutive hours.


00:31:40.121 --> 00:31:43.839
At the time Miller disappeared,
Elmer was in a steamy private chat...


00:31:43.999 --> 00:31:47.638
...with the first tenor of the
Men's Chorus of Greater Tacoma.


00:31:47.798 --> 00:31:49.837
It still felt good arresting him.


00:32:11.509 --> 00:32:13.349
<i>- Hello?
- I caught you.</i>


00:32:13.988 --> 00:32:17.707
<i>- Barely. I've got a big date tonight.
- Big, special or big, large?</i>


00:32:17.867 --> 00:32:21.705
I don't know. I haven't met Peggy
the secretary yet. What's up?


00:32:21.865 --> 00:32:25.544
<i>I had a thought. Remember that
Andrew Kilburn guy and his review?</i>


00:32:25.703 --> 00:32:27.383
Yeah, sure. What about it?


00:32:27.663 --> 00:32:30.062
Well, why use his account?


00:32:30.262 --> 00:32:33.820
I mean, maybe it wasn't random.
Maybe they know each other.


00:32:34.301 --> 00:32:36.419
<i>- Yeah, it's possible.
- Yeah.</i>


00:32:36.579 --> 00:32:39.578
<i>- All right. I'll see you Sunday.
- Wait, Sunday?</i>


00:32:40.898 --> 00:32:41.978
Annie's birthday.


00:32:42.617 --> 00:32:45.536
Oh, shit, I forgot.


00:32:45.696 --> 00:32:48.000
<i>- Okay, can I bring a date?
- Are you kidding?</i>


00:32:48.215 --> 00:32:50.174
You don't even know
if you like this girl.


00:32:50.335 --> 00:32:53.653
No, not Peggy. Melanie.
She's a social worker.


00:32:53.813 --> 00:32:56.292
She likes sushi and rock-climbing
and Dickens.


00:32:56.452 --> 00:32:59.931
<i>- I can't believe you.
- It's a numbers game.</i>


00:33:00.091 --> 00:33:02.610
<i>Fine, fine. I gotta go.</i>


00:33:02.770 --> 00:33:05.089
Okay. Hey, you got a date?


00:33:05.249 --> 00:33:09.087
<i>- Good night.
- Okay. Bye. Good night, Sam.</i>


00:33:22.563 --> 00:33:24.346
Molly gave me
a birthday present already.


00:33:24.522 --> 00:33:26.321
It's a computer game
that I downloaded.


00:33:26.481 --> 00:33:29.400
- It's about horses.
- How sweet of her. That looks like fun.


00:33:30.360 --> 00:33:32.279
Not really. It's kind of silly.


00:33:33.238 --> 00:33:37.397
- I'll show it to you later.
- Okay, honey. I love you. Gotta run.


00:34:07.386 --> 00:34:10.224
Come on, Annie. Let me get one first.


00:34:12.344 --> 00:34:13.943
Somebody order a bunch of pizzas?


00:34:14.103 --> 00:34:15.422
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:34:15.583 --> 00:34:17.626
- Hey, Griffin.
- For the birthday girl. Hello.


00:34:17.742 --> 00:34:20.461
- How are you? Over here?
- Over here.


00:34:23.060 --> 00:34:26.179
Listen, I only made it through
a few months of Kilburn's posts.


00:34:26.339 --> 00:34:28.122
- We'll need more bodies on this.
- Okay.


00:34:28.218 --> 00:34:32.777
He blogged, he uploaded vids, he
built sites. He practically lived online.


00:34:32.976 --> 00:34:35.816
- What, not anymore?
- Not since he died...


00:34:36.015 --> 00:34:39.214
...of something called
diabetic ketoacidosis.


00:34:39.374 --> 00:34:42.572
Which is what happens when you
don't take your insulin for a few days.


00:34:42.732 --> 00:34:45.532
Anyway, an hour after his body
was found...


00:34:45.692 --> 00:34:46.811
...Kill With Me went up.


00:34:46.971 --> 00:34:49.809
And an hour after that, Kilburn's
review was spammed Web-wide.


00:34:49.970 --> 00:34:53.688
- And you think our guy killed him?
- The ME called it a suicide.


00:35:18.040 --> 00:35:19.199
Hi.


00:35:19.359 --> 00:35:20.958
You're right on time.


00:35:21.118 --> 00:35:24.597
Yeah, well, it's a curse.
I spend half my life waiting for people.


00:35:24.757 --> 00:35:27.756
So... Dave Williams.


00:35:30.394 --> 00:35:34.673
That's a great address, by the way.
Eights bring prosperity.


00:35:34.833 --> 00:35:37.592
- I didn't know that.
- Yeah.


00:35:38.392 --> 00:35:40.431
- Come in.
- Thanks.


00:35:55.665 --> 00:35:56.665
Here you go, honey.


00:35:56.825 --> 00:35:58.784
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.


00:36:03.342 --> 00:36:04.422
Detective.


00:36:04.622 --> 00:36:06.661
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:36:06.821 --> 00:36:10.020
Griffin invited me
to his birthday party.


00:36:11.500 --> 00:36:13.579
Yeah. Kind of a young crowd.


00:36:13.738 --> 00:36:15.738
Kind of a young crowd, Griffin.


00:36:15.898 --> 00:36:18.617
- Well, do you skate?
- No.


00:36:18.777 --> 00:36:20.696
- Thank you.
- Yeah, go ahead.


00:36:20.896 --> 00:36:23.615
Look, I'm gonna get out of here.
I'm sorry.


00:36:23.775 --> 00:36:27.453
You just got here. Don't go.
Have some pizza.


00:36:27.613 --> 00:36:30.452
Come on. It's not that bad.


00:36:39.729 --> 00:36:42.768
Wow, you must really like Asia, huh?


00:36:44.688 --> 00:36:46.447
Just Korea.


00:36:48.725 --> 00:36:50.365
Korea.


00:36:50.845 --> 00:36:52.724
Well, it's fabulous.


00:36:53.884 --> 00:36:55.403
Thank you.


00:36:58.082 --> 00:36:59.922
So you gonna let me see them?


00:37:00.481 --> 00:37:02.120
Of course.


00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:04.440
Through the kitchen.


00:37:07.478 --> 00:37:11.517
I gotta tell you, a 710 Pullman
and a 712 Observation Car?


00:37:11.677 --> 00:37:13.720
My heart skipped a beat
when I got your e-mail.


00:37:13.877 --> 00:37:17.875
- If they're really in mint condition...
- My dad and I hardly ever used them.


00:37:18.395 --> 00:37:22.433
We mostly played foosball
and we built things.


00:37:23.792 --> 00:37:26.671
Toys, contraptions.


00:37:27.192 --> 00:37:29.150
We had a workshop.


00:37:29.791 --> 00:37:31.629
He died last year.


00:37:34.269 --> 00:37:37.148
Well, I'm sorry.


00:37:50.662 --> 00:37:53.741
Annie, would you come over here
for a second? Bring your skates.


00:37:53.902 --> 00:37:56.860
- Okay.
- I want you to meet someone.


00:37:59.219 --> 00:38:02.139
This is Annie, the birthday girl.
This is my friend, Eric.


00:38:02.338 --> 00:38:04.058
- Hello, Annie.
- Hi.


00:38:04.218 --> 00:38:05.977
- Happy birthday.
- Thanks.


00:38:06.417 --> 00:38:08.216
You must be, what, 8?


00:38:08.736 --> 00:38:11.095
How did you know?
Everyone else thinks I'm older.


00:38:12.374 --> 00:38:13.774
Well, I'm a detective.


00:38:15.613 --> 00:38:17.933
- Are you ready to go skating finally?
- I think.


00:38:33.847 --> 00:38:35.806
I sure hope you like it.


00:38:35.966 --> 00:38:37.525
It's a punching bag.


00:38:37.686 --> 00:38:38.885
Okay, so you blow it up...


00:38:39.045 --> 00:38:41.164
...and whenever you
get in a really bad mood...


00:38:41.364 --> 00:38:42.843
...you sock it in the head.


00:38:44.123 --> 00:38:45.122
Can I do karate on it?


00:38:45.282 --> 00:38:49.281
Of course you can. You can do karate,
kung fu, tae kwon do.


00:38:49.441 --> 00:38:52.320
- Thank you, Griffin.
- You're welcome, sweetie.


00:38:52.519 --> 00:38:53.799
That might be my date.


00:38:55.919 --> 00:38:57.398
Mom.


00:38:59.437 --> 00:39:01.356
Oh, come on.


00:39:01.956 --> 00:39:03.116
Happy birthday, sweetie.


00:39:03.276 --> 00:39:04.395
- Have fun.
- Thanks.


00:39:06.354 --> 00:39:08.194
Sweetheart...


00:39:08.674 --> 00:39:09.593
...I gotta go.


00:39:09.833 --> 00:39:12.513
It's a real emergency, or I
would never leave you like this.


00:39:12.712 --> 00:39:15.551
- I'll make it up to you, I promise. Okay?
- Okay.


00:39:18.150 --> 00:39:20.069
I'm looking for Griffin Dowd. He's...


00:39:20.229 --> 00:39:21.189
- Yeah. Hi.
- Hi.


00:39:21.349 --> 00:39:23.069
- I'm Melanie.
- Oh, yes. Hi, Melanie.


00:39:23.268 --> 00:39:26.267
Wow, you are gorgeous.
I'm sorry. I've gotta run.


00:39:55.896 --> 00:39:57.415
Todd!


00:39:58.135 --> 00:40:00.134
Isn't that your dad?


00:40:08.172 --> 00:40:11.210
- Same build, same coloring.
- The counter's faster than last time.


00:40:11.890 --> 00:40:13.409
Yeah.


00:40:14.409 --> 00:40:16.322
I swear I've seen this guy
somewhere before.


00:40:16.488 --> 00:40:18.408
- Yeah.
- We all have. He's David Williams.


00:40:18.607 --> 00:40:20.526
He used to be
a reporter for Channel 12.


00:40:20.806 --> 00:40:22.886
He now hosts a TV show
on public access.


00:40:23.086 --> 00:40:24.845
Call Bagley.
Set up a press conference.


00:40:25.005 --> 00:40:27.524
Sir, wait just a minute, please.


00:40:27.884 --> 00:40:30.683
This is what he wants. Anything
you say will promote the site.


00:40:30.843 --> 00:40:32.962
That's a possibility,
but what would you prefer?


00:40:33.162 --> 00:40:34.681
Talk to National Security Agency.


00:40:34.841 --> 00:40:37.521
Their computer capability's
beyond ours. We need their help.


00:40:37.680 --> 00:40:40.159
That's fine, but I've got
a man being publicly tortured.


00:40:40.360 --> 00:40:43.638
How will it look if he dies and the
Bureau never tried to help the guy?


00:40:43.798 --> 00:40:47.396
Not as bad as if we reach out
and it kills him faster.


00:40:48.396 --> 00:40:50.916
You honestly believe
that could happen?


00:40:52.754 --> 00:40:54.274
Yes, sir, I do.


00:41:02.431 --> 00:41:03.671
I'm sorry, Marsh.


00:41:05.390 --> 00:41:07.029
I got no choice.


00:41:33.348 --> 00:41:35.898
<i>We're gathered here
to share some information...</i>


00:41:35.899 --> 00:41:37.697
<i>... in regards to criminal conduct...</i>


00:41:37.698 --> 00:41:40.437
<i>... that originated in the
Portland metropolitan area...</i>


00:41:40.497 --> 00:41:43.496
<i>... but that has
far-reaching implications.</i>


00:41:43.497 --> 00:41:45.694
<i>Let me introduce
Special Agent-in-Charge...</i>


00:41:45.695 --> 00:41:47.975
<i>... of the FBI's Portland field
office...</i>


00:41:48.174 --> 00:41:50.054
...Richard Brooks.


00:41:51.373 --> 00:41:52.852
Thank you, chief.


00:41:53.852 --> 00:41:57.371
<i>A week ago, a man was killed
in this city.</i>


00:41:58.251 --> 00:42:02.808
<i>This barbaric, cowardly murder
was streamed live on the Internet.</i>


00:42:02.968 --> 00:42:06.687
<i>As part of the killer's design, the more
people who logged on to the site...</i>


00:42:06.888 --> 00:42:11.126
<i>... to witness the victim's suffering,
the sooner the victim died.</i>


00:42:11.127 --> 00:42:13.604
<i>Millions of Americans
chose to visit the site...</i>


00:42:13.605 --> 00:42:18.083
<i>... believing that they were witnessing
a mere hoax, a stunt or a prank.</i>


00:42:18.243 --> 00:42:19.895
<i>Well, unfortunately, it wasn't.</i>


00:42:19.962 --> 00:42:21.522
<i>Today a second individual...</i>


00:42:21.523 --> 00:42:24.639
<i>... has appeared on the site
and his life, too, is in jeopardy.</i>


00:42:24.640 --> 00:42:27.919
<i>The victim is the doting father
of two boys...</i>


00:42:29.719 --> 00:42:31.958
<i>... a loving husband of 22 years...</i>


00:42:32.157 --> 00:42:35.548
<i>... and a devoted son. In other words,
he's a good American, one of us.</i>


00:42:35.637 --> 00:42:39.595
<i>The torture that he is experiencing
now is unimaginable in its cruelty.</i>


00:42:40.315 --> 00:42:41.750
<i>We're doing what we can...</i>


00:42:41.754 --> 00:42:44.754
<i>... to shut down the site
and bring the killer to justice.</i>


00:42:44.993 --> 00:42:47.993
<i>In the meantime, we ask that
everyone stay away from the site.</i>


00:42:48.432 --> 00:42:50.431
Any visit to this site,
no matter how brief...


00:42:50.591 --> 00:42:52.551
...will only hasten the victim's death.


00:42:54.549 --> 00:42:57.909
Any American who visits the site
is an accomplice to murder.


00:42:58.068 --> 00:43:00.427
<i>We are the murder weapon.</i>


00:43:00.587 --> 00:43:04.186
<i>- We ask that you spread the word...
- Let's main-screen the website.</i>


00:43:05.426 --> 00:43:08.264
Hey, Tim, I think
he's trying to say something.


00:43:12.343 --> 00:43:14.502
Eight... Eight...


00:43:17.021 --> 00:43:19.340
Eight, eight, eight.


00:43:19.900 --> 00:43:21.900
Oh, I get it. It's an address, I think.


00:43:22.499 --> 00:43:26.337
Eight... Eight-oh-eight...


00:43:26.538 --> 00:43:28.097
...Newberry.
- Newberry?


00:43:28.297 --> 00:43:30.176
There's a Newberry Road
in Laurelhurst.


00:43:54.688 --> 00:43:55.687
Police! Open the door!


00:44:15.959 --> 00:44:17.679
Basement's here!


00:44:30.714 --> 00:44:31.713
It's the wrong house.


00:44:39.197 --> 00:44:42.268
<i>- Any American who visits the site...
- He was here, though.</i>


00:44:42.269 --> 00:44:45.348
<i>... is an accomplice to murder.
We are the murder weapon.</i>


00:44:45.549 --> 00:44:49.347
<i>Any American who visits the site
is an accomplice to murder.</i>


00:44:49.546 --> 00:44:52.226
<i>We are the murder weapon.
Any American...</i>


00:44:52.386 --> 00:44:55.545
All right. We should send
Forensics in here.


00:44:57.184 --> 00:45:00.743
<i>Any American who visits the site
is an accomplice to murder.</i>


00:45:00.903 --> 00:45:03.622
<i>We are the murder weapon.</i>


00:45:08.899 --> 00:45:13.697
Yeah, I understand that. Just
have her check it again, okay?


00:45:13.858 --> 00:45:16.976
- Six hours. So fast.
- Twice as fast as Miller.


00:45:17.217 --> 00:45:19.575
Nobody thinks
they did anything wrong.


00:45:20.255 --> 00:45:24.533
Why should they?
They're curious about a website.


00:45:25.014 --> 00:45:27.373
You check the headlines,
check the stock market...


00:45:27.572 --> 00:45:29.492
...watch some strangers have sex.


00:45:29.972 --> 00:45:32.411
See a journalist get his head cut off.


00:45:35.130 --> 00:45:37.769
When did the world
go so fucking insane?


00:45:40.248 --> 00:45:42.767
You've been working
the streets too long.


00:45:43.446 --> 00:45:47.405
He was definitely here.
He just got moved and didn't know it.


00:45:51.403 --> 00:45:53.963
So Mrs. Williams is checking her
husband's e-mail for us.


00:45:56.162 --> 00:45:59.600
She says he was contacted about the
trains through the public TV website.


00:46:00.840 --> 00:46:04.479
I guess in his bio, he mentions he's
a collector. That was about a week ago.


00:46:04.958 --> 00:46:06.039
Who owns the house?


00:46:06.198 --> 00:46:11.797
Tom Park, 60s, widower. He's out
of town visiting family in South Korea.


00:46:11.956 --> 00:46:14.995
He runs a local market here.
He makes the trip every year.


00:46:15.555 --> 00:46:17.754
So our guy's a customer.


00:46:18.074 --> 00:46:20.953
We're trying to get ahold of Mr. Park,
see if he knows anything.


00:46:21.113 --> 00:46:24.112
We'll do a canvass. Seems like
a pretty tight-knit community.


00:46:24.272 --> 00:46:25.790
Maybe somebody saw something.


00:47:38.204 --> 00:47:39.763
Did you see this?


00:47:42.722 --> 00:47:44.961
On the bright side, along with
every other daily...


00:47:45.121 --> 00:47:47.120
...they're not printing
the name of the site.


00:47:47.280 --> 00:47:49.120
Well, isn't that noble?


00:47:49.320 --> 00:47:50.439
A little late, though.


00:47:52.279 --> 00:47:55.357
Did Annie ever forgive you
for bailing on the party?


00:47:55.718 --> 00:47:59.396
Yeah. After 11 bedtime stories.
Thank you.


00:48:00.636 --> 00:48:04.234
You know, when we first met,
I knew you looked familiar.


00:48:07.033 --> 00:48:08.912
Nick and I came up together.


00:48:11.712 --> 00:48:14.231
Nick Haskins.
That was Annie's father, right?


00:48:15.230 --> 00:48:16.989
Did he introduce us?


00:48:18.109 --> 00:48:21.588
No. No, we never met.
I saw you at the funeral.


00:48:23.667 --> 00:48:25.226
Right.


00:48:30.344 --> 00:48:34.063
Anyway, he was a...
He was a great guy.


00:48:34.903 --> 00:48:37.421
Yeah, he was a great guy.


00:48:46.738 --> 00:48:49.777
<i>It's apparent our subject
is extremely organized...</i>


00:48:49.937 --> 00:48:51.617
...and sophisticated.


00:48:51.777 --> 00:48:54.336
And based upon his ability
to subdue his victims...


00:48:54.496 --> 00:48:57.135
...transport them and maintain
physical control over them...


00:48:57.294 --> 00:49:00.893
...in a private setting, I'd describe
the offender as highly capable.


00:49:01.053 --> 00:49:02.932
Remember, he's not going
after easy prey.


00:49:03.092 --> 00:49:05.411
These abductions leave him exposed.


00:49:05.612 --> 00:49:08.770
Even the kitten he stole
in broad daylight. Why the risks?


00:49:08.931 --> 00:49:13.488
Because each of these actions was
absolutely essential to his purpose.


00:49:13.648 --> 00:49:16.087
You wanna catch him,
understand his goals.


00:49:16.287 --> 00:49:18.166
You know, this guy...


00:49:18.367 --> 00:49:20.726
...he's the same as
the Unabomber, Tim McVeigh.


00:49:20.926 --> 00:49:23.100
He's another terrorist
trying to make a statement.


00:49:23.245 --> 00:49:26.963
Maybe. Still, it goes back to his goals.
Why kill these particular people?


00:49:27.284 --> 00:49:29.603
And why is he killing them
on the Internet?


00:49:29.763 --> 00:49:33.202
My guess, none of it's random.
None of it.


00:49:38.439 --> 00:49:43.638
Okay. Every post Kilburn ever left.
Thousands. And a couple of DVDs.


00:49:43.837 --> 00:49:47.996
One for you, one for me. Every
video clip that he ever uploaded.


00:49:48.156 --> 00:49:51.474
That was his real hobby, was
pulling the sick shit off the Net...


00:49:51.674 --> 00:49:54.793
...and then posting it
on shock-video sites.


00:49:55.553 --> 00:49:58.832
Anyways, this is the last post
before he died.


00:49:59.191 --> 00:50:01.111
It's sort of a best-of compilation...


00:50:01.271 --> 00:50:03.710
...something he called
"The Best of the Worst."


00:50:09.747 --> 00:50:10.827
Oh, yeah.


00:50:13.227 --> 00:50:15.945
Poor Kilburn. He had so much
to offer the world.


00:50:16.105 --> 00:50:17.265
Yeah.


00:50:17.625 --> 00:50:21.263
I got four more bodies from Brooks,
so let's share the pain, shall we?


00:50:21.423 --> 00:50:22.823
Great.


00:51:16.202 --> 00:51:17.963
Okay.


00:52:07.664 --> 00:52:11.262
Mom. TiVo's not working.


00:52:11.423 --> 00:52:14.421
Okay, honey.
Look, I'll be out in a minute.


00:52:43.010 --> 00:52:45.929
Mom, there's a video of our house
on the computer.


00:52:46.130 --> 00:52:49.288
Watch whatever you want, honey.
I'll be right out.


00:53:24.475 --> 00:53:26.754
Hey, Griff. Good morning.


00:53:41.069 --> 00:53:42.069
Annie.


00:53:51.265 --> 00:53:52.824
Annie!


00:53:54.624 --> 00:53:56.343
- Annie!
- Mom?


00:54:00.502 --> 00:54:03.500
Baby, what are you doing out here?
What are you doing outside?


00:54:03.660 --> 00:54:05.939
I was just gonna ride my bike
for the camera.


00:54:06.099 --> 00:54:08.099
You stay with Grandma.


00:54:19.735 --> 00:54:21.934
Hey. Hey, that's evidence.


00:54:22.133 --> 00:54:24.933
- I'm sorry. My daughter, she...
- It's okay. We're here now.


00:54:25.093 --> 00:54:27.852
It's okay.
Do you know whose car this is?


00:54:28.011 --> 00:54:30.571
Yeah, I think I have an idea
whose car this is.


00:54:36.248 --> 00:54:37.767
God.


00:55:13.994 --> 00:55:16.753
Annie thought she'd downloaded
a game from one of her friends.


00:55:16.913 --> 00:55:18.153
It had a backdoor Trojan.


00:55:18.313 --> 00:55:21.231
It got him all the way
into my wireless network.


00:55:21.791 --> 00:55:23.871
Which means that he has access
to all my files.


00:55:47.821 --> 00:55:50.621
Call me when you get there.
I love you.


00:56:02.057 --> 00:56:04.056
Why don't you just go with them?


00:56:05.295 --> 00:56:07.014
What are you waiting for?


00:56:09.094 --> 00:56:10.974
And do what? Hide out?


00:56:11.933 --> 00:56:13.452
That's right.


00:56:14.012 --> 00:56:16.891
I think you've sacrificed enough
already, don't you?


00:56:18.890 --> 00:56:20.810
Nobody's gonna blame you
for taking cover.


00:56:20.970 --> 00:56:23.368
The piece of shit's camped out
on your front lawn.


00:56:23.729 --> 00:56:26.288
Annie's already lost one parent
to the job, so...


00:56:26.448 --> 00:56:30.206
...yeah. Get lost.


00:56:33.725 --> 00:56:35.484
Just my opinion.


00:57:02.354 --> 00:57:05.552
<i>- Yeah?
- Hey, Jen. Did they get off okay?</i>


00:57:05.712 --> 00:57:09.391
<i>Yeah. The Bureau's gonna put
them up a couple hours away.</i>


00:57:09.551 --> 00:57:12.030
<i>And I'm gonna stay someplace
closer to work.</i>


00:57:12.190 --> 00:57:16.069
Good. So you wanna hear my theory
why he did this?


00:57:16.269 --> 00:57:17.268
Of course.


00:57:17.429 --> 00:57:20.107
<i>There is a connection
between him and Kilburn...</i>


00:57:20.267 --> 00:57:23.786
<i>... and he knows you're leading
the team to find it.</i>


00:57:24.065 --> 00:57:26.065
I think I might know what
that connection is.


00:57:26.225 --> 00:57:28.544
Emphasis on "might."
A few things I gotta check out.


00:57:28.705 --> 00:57:30.184
I'm on my way in. Are you coming?


00:57:31.143 --> 00:57:32.422
I need a couple hours.


00:57:32.504 --> 00:57:34.141
<i>I'll see you at the office.</i>


00:57:34.142 --> 00:57:35.707
Okay, I'll show you
what I got then.


00:57:35.861 --> 00:57:37.221
Okay.


00:57:40.939 --> 00:57:43.779
<i>- Griffin Dowd.
- Hi. It's Melanie.</i>


00:57:45.578 --> 00:57:49.217
Melanie, hi. I didn't think
I'd hear from you again.


00:57:49.496 --> 00:57:52.256
<i>Your e-mail was very sweet.</i>


00:57:52.416 --> 00:57:55.094
Thank you. Yeah, I spent
a lot of time on that one.


00:57:56.973 --> 00:57:59.973
So I heard you hung out
at the roller rink.


00:58:00.132 --> 00:58:02.092
Even had some cake?


00:58:02.491 --> 00:58:05.490
<i>Two pieces. But don't tell anybody.</i>


00:58:05.650 --> 00:58:07.969
Okay, well,
your secret is safe with me.


00:58:08.129 --> 00:58:11.288
<i>Annie really liked you, and
you know what they say about kids.</i>


00:58:11.489 --> 00:58:14.807
<i>Along with dogs, they're terrific
judges of character.</i>


00:58:15.687 --> 00:58:18.606
What can I say?
I would have to agree.


00:58:19.566 --> 00:58:21.765
I'm a total catch.


00:58:29.361 --> 00:58:30.841
Hi, Ray.


00:58:45.356 --> 00:58:47.714
- Where's Griffin?
- Haven't seen him.


00:58:48.554 --> 00:58:50.313
Brooks wants to see you.


00:58:50.474 --> 00:58:52.113
- Now?
- Now.


00:59:29.379 --> 00:59:32.379
- Agent Marsh, sir.
- Yeah, send her in.


00:59:36.097 --> 00:59:38.017
You wanted to see me, sir?


00:59:38.536 --> 00:59:40.215
How are you doing?


00:59:40.655 --> 00:59:44.493
Well, it was an interesting start
of the day. We're fine.


00:59:45.373 --> 00:59:46.812
Good.


00:59:47.092 --> 00:59:49.332
I want you to know
I did follow up with the NSA.


00:59:49.532 --> 00:59:52.850
As far as using their supercomputer
goes, unfortunately the answer's no.


00:59:54.690 --> 00:59:57.409
- Why not?
- They're barred for domestic use.


00:59:57.569 --> 01:00:01.448
Domestic? We've got him using
mirrors in Russia, Malaysia...


01:00:01.607 --> 01:00:04.526
It's too public a forum. They
don't want their capabilities known.


01:00:04.726 --> 01:00:06.086
As far as what they can and...


01:00:24.119 --> 01:00:26.758
It's Griffin. It's Griffin!


01:00:31.396 --> 01:00:33.796
Where do these tubes lead?
What are those tanks?


01:00:33.956 --> 01:00:35.595
Tim! Punch in on those tanks.


01:00:38.594 --> 01:00:40.193
What's that say?


01:00:40.393 --> 01:00:41.432
"Sulfuric acid"?


01:00:42.432 --> 01:00:43.711
Sulfuric acid?


01:00:49.349 --> 01:00:51.029
If that's water in that tank...


01:00:51.589 --> 01:00:54.188
...pretty soon he's gonna be
sitting in battery acid.


01:01:28.215 --> 01:01:30.374
Don't wanna hear about
bureaus and jurisdictions.


01:01:30.534 --> 01:01:33.093
This is domestic terrorism,
plain and simple.


01:01:35.213 --> 01:01:38.611
Yeah? Well, just get it done.
Yeah. All right.


01:01:52.526 --> 01:01:56.165
You know, if no one was watching
right now, you'd just be sitting in water.


01:02:00.083 --> 01:02:03.842
But the whole world wants to watch
you die, and they don't even know you.


01:02:22.554 --> 01:02:24.794
It's so fast this time.


01:02:26.234 --> 01:02:28.472
It's word of mouth, I guess.


01:02:30.032 --> 01:02:32.111
Because I let you keep your badge on.


01:03:41.526 --> 01:03:44.405
Ray! I need your help.


01:03:50.003 --> 01:03:52.281
Tim, go in on his eyes.


01:03:56.479 --> 01:04:00.119
I think he's trying to say something
to us. Here.


01:04:00.758 --> 01:04:04.037
Please. Do your best. Hurry!


01:04:07.796 --> 01:04:09.835
Right eye's dots.


01:04:09.995 --> 01:04:12.434
Left is... Left is dashes.


01:04:20.031 --> 01:04:21.511
"S."


01:04:33.186 --> 01:04:34.706
"I."


01:04:38.784 --> 01:04:40.144
"D."


01:05:11.611 --> 01:05:13.571
<i>There aren't any other kids here...</i>


01:05:13.731 --> 01:05:16.610
<i>... but the swimming pool's fun
and there's satellite TV.</i>


01:05:17.249 --> 01:05:19.209
<i>Mom, are you there?</i>


01:05:21.404 --> 01:05:23.606
<i>We miss you, Mommy.
When are you coming?</i>


01:05:23.607 --> 01:05:27.766
<i>It's starting to get really boring.
Your work isn't done yet?</i>


01:05:28.406 --> 01:05:30.165
I wish.


01:05:32.725 --> 01:05:34.243
<i>Mom?</i>


01:05:35.163 --> 01:05:36.206
I have to go now, honey.


01:05:36.563 --> 01:05:39.082
Listen, you call me
as soon as you wake up. Okay, bug?


01:05:39.242 --> 01:05:42.640
<i>- It's Box.
- I will. Love you. Say hi to Griffin.</i>


01:05:42.800 --> 01:05:46.438
I love you too, honey. Bye.


01:06:09.910 --> 01:06:11.549
Dinner.


01:06:21.226 --> 01:06:23.665
I think I'll take a shower first.


01:06:53.454 --> 01:06:58.652
The acid was stolen from a research
lab at Marshall Junior College.


01:07:01.131 --> 01:07:04.330
The thief apparently knew
his way around.


01:07:07.569 --> 01:07:11.848
Looks like... Looks like Griffin
was baited with a phone call.


01:07:12.007 --> 01:07:15.725
But we can't trace it because
it was made with a spoof card.


01:07:15.886 --> 01:07:18.565
Yeah, it's a phone card.
Costs about 10 bucks an hour.


01:07:18.724 --> 01:07:21.603
Lets you program any
caller ID you want.


01:07:22.763 --> 01:07:26.442
This guy breached my laptop.
He must've owned Griffin's too.


01:07:26.602 --> 01:07:29.000
Figured out where he was vulnerable.


01:07:34.199 --> 01:07:35.878
Sorry.


01:07:39.077 --> 01:07:41.676
I'm good at a lot of things, you know?


01:07:42.595 --> 01:07:44.995
But I'm not good at losing people.


01:07:45.155 --> 01:07:47.953
I'm bad at losing people.


01:08:56.808 --> 01:08:58.447
Rush-hour suicide.


01:08:59.607 --> 01:09:03.966
I'm pretty sure that's what Griffin was
trying to say. I'm just not sure why.


01:09:07.044 --> 01:09:08.724
Yeah, I remember.


01:09:08.884 --> 01:09:11.803
He was a professor, that guy.


01:09:12.242 --> 01:09:15.561
Andrew Kilburn included this
in his greatest hits.


01:09:17.561 --> 01:09:21.439
- I was just there, like a week ago.
- Where?


01:09:21.679 --> 01:09:25.717
At the Bridge Diner. You know, the
one under the Broadway Bridge.


01:09:26.317 --> 01:09:28.876
I was talking to Scotty Hillman...


01:09:29.036 --> 01:09:31.355
...the guy who owned the cat.
That's where he works.


01:09:32.954 --> 01:09:35.194
What was this guy's name?
Do you remember?


01:09:36.634 --> 01:09:40.072
No. I think
he taught Chemistry, though.


01:09:42.871 --> 01:09:45.310
At Marshall Junior College?


01:09:52.627 --> 01:09:56.665
Andrew Kilburn, a sophomore at
Portland State. Died last month...


01:09:56.825 --> 01:10:00.264
...but that didn't stop him
from recommending, after he died...


01:10:00.424 --> 01:10:03.663
...a new website called
killwithme.com.


01:10:03.983 --> 01:10:07.902
How'd he do that? He didn't.
The killer did, using his account.


01:10:08.061 --> 01:10:10.700
When Agent Griffin Dowd's
investigation revealed why...


01:10:10.861 --> 01:10:12.900
...this deceased college student
was chosen...


01:10:13.060 --> 01:10:17.058
...to promote the Kill With Me site,
it cost him his life.


01:10:21.137 --> 01:10:23.336
This is James Reilly.


01:10:23.656 --> 01:10:24.855
Sixteen months ago...


01:10:25.016 --> 01:10:27.934
...depressed over the recent death
of his wife, a hematologist...


01:10:28.094 --> 01:10:32.133
...Reilly staggered out into rush-hour
traffic on the Broadway Bridge.


01:10:32.293 --> 01:10:34.132
Traffic copters were out in force...


01:10:34.292 --> 01:10:37.051
...but only one caught all the action
from beginning to end...


01:10:37.211 --> 01:10:38.570
...Channel 12.


01:10:39.210 --> 01:10:42.689
The regular pilot was out sick that day,
so the job went to Herbert Miller.


01:10:44.128 --> 01:10:48.806
He later told friends he'd gotten lucky.
At the right place at the right time.


01:10:53.405 --> 01:10:54.844
The back of Reilly's skull...


01:10:55.004 --> 01:10:58.403
...landed on the rooftop
of this diner. So did his glasses.


01:10:58.563 --> 01:11:00.442
The skull was turned over
to the coroner...


01:11:00.602 --> 01:11:03.961
...but the glasses were retrieved
by one of the diner's employees...


01:11:04.121 --> 01:11:05.280
...Scotty Hillman.


01:11:06.080 --> 01:11:07.919
He put them up for sale online.


01:11:08.080 --> 01:11:09.758
And they sold quickly.


01:11:09.918 --> 01:11:12.118
Kids were home from school.
Parents were outraged.


01:11:12.278 --> 01:11:14.717
They called the TV stations.
The TV stations apologized.


01:11:14.877 --> 01:11:16.236
Except for Channel 12.


01:11:16.396 --> 01:11:19.715
They'd been having a little problem
in the ratings, but not that afternoon.


01:11:19.875 --> 01:11:21.434
Their numbers were sky-high.


01:11:21.594 --> 01:11:24.033
And knowing a good thing
when it fell into their lap...


01:11:24.193 --> 01:11:26.392
...they rushed a veteran reporter
to the scene.


01:11:26.393 --> 01:11:27.871
<i>This is David Williams...</i>


01:11:27.872 --> 01:11:30.590
He got lucky, landed an interview
with a local businessman...


01:11:30.751 --> 01:11:33.670
...whose parked Cadillac had been
struck by Reilly's falling body.


01:11:33.870 --> 01:11:35.069
When the interview ended...


01:11:35.229 --> 01:11:38.108
...Channel 12, as a courtesy to
those who might have missed it...


01:11:38.268 --> 01:11:40.547
...aired the entire video one last time.


01:11:40.707 --> 01:11:43.346
Within minutes, Andrew Kilburn
had pulled it off his TiVo...


01:11:43.506 --> 01:11:46.505
...and posted it on five different
shock-video sites.


01:11:46.665 --> 01:11:49.663
From there, Reilly's suicide
was public domain.


01:11:49.864 --> 01:11:54.782
Something for five billion people
to feed on, laugh at, gossip about.


01:11:54.942 --> 01:11:56.781
Reilly had a son, Owen.


01:11:57.861 --> 01:12:01.100
He was brilliant. Good at electronics,
mechanics and computers...


01:12:01.260 --> 01:12:04.458
<i>... but he was disturbed.
He was troubled. He was withdrawn.</i>


01:12:05.058 --> 01:12:07.297
Owen took his father's suicide
very hard.


01:12:07.458 --> 01:12:11.096
He had to be hospitalized.
And six months ago he was released.


01:12:11.816 --> 01:12:14.575
This x-ray image is supposed to be
Owen's father.


01:12:14.735 --> 01:12:17.334
The number on the left,
the date his father died...


01:12:18.294 --> 01:12:21.412
...followed by the number
of his autopsy report.


01:12:21.812 --> 01:12:24.571
<i>Owen lives alone now
at his father's house in Fairview.</i>


01:12:24.731 --> 01:12:26.930
What do you say we arrest
the piece of shit?


01:12:28.689 --> 01:12:30.289
Go! Go!


01:13:04.396 --> 01:13:05.635
Basement's clear!


01:13:20.070 --> 01:13:21.789
This is bad.


01:13:53.722 --> 01:13:57.055
<i>There are new developments
in the Internet murder investigation...</i>


01:13:57.056 --> 01:14:00.574
<i>... tonight out of Portland, Oregon.
For more, let's turn to Marilyn Deutsch.</i>


01:14:00.575 --> 01:14:03.373
<i>Right. Police now say they know
who is kidnapping people...</i>


01:14:03.374 --> 01:14:06.173
<i>... in this area and then killing them
live on the Web.</i>


01:14:06.533 --> 01:14:10.132
<i>Take a look at this picture. Police say
the suspect's name is Owen Reilly.</i>


01:14:10.292 --> 01:14:13.930
<i>He is 20 years old,
and just nine months ago...</i>


01:14:14.610 --> 01:14:16.169
First...


01:14:16.329 --> 01:14:19.688
...I just wanted to say how sorry I am.


01:14:20.248 --> 01:14:22.927
This was a loss for all of us...


01:14:23.086 --> 01:14:26.166
...but most deeply for you,
and we know that. I know that.


01:14:28.205 --> 01:14:32.563
You've done everything you
possibly could. You've given enough.


01:14:33.723 --> 01:14:37.201
- I want you to take some time off.
- What?


01:14:37.681 --> 01:14:40.640
Why? Because now it's personal?


01:14:40.840 --> 01:14:43.014
This guy's still running around,
the case is open.


01:14:43.159 --> 01:14:44.478
The kid's face is everywhere.


01:14:44.638 --> 01:14:47.838
He's driving around in a 40-year-old
VW bus with electronics in it.


01:14:48.037 --> 01:14:49.646
We'll have him
by this time tomorrow.


01:14:49.797 --> 01:14:52.995
- Maybe.
- Jennifer, I'm not only thinking of you.


01:14:54.395 --> 01:14:57.554
Now join your family. Just for a week.


01:14:59.833 --> 01:15:01.873
I'll take a day.


01:15:50.054 --> 01:15:52.294
- Hey.
- Hey.


01:15:52.813 --> 01:15:55.732
So, what'd he say?


01:15:56.492 --> 01:15:58.492
He told me to get lost.


01:16:00.091 --> 01:16:01.410
Well, he's right.


01:16:04.169 --> 01:16:06.208
And what did you say?


01:16:11.886 --> 01:16:13.645
That's what I figured.


01:18:01.446 --> 01:18:04.004
<i>This has been America News Radio.</i>


01:18:04.164 --> 01:18:07.524
<i>Now back to your local
ANR station for news.</i>


01:18:08.123 --> 01:18:10.722
<i>Good evening.
You're listening to KMZR, Portland.</i>


01:18:10.882 --> 01:18:13.721
<i>This is the news at the top
of the 10:00 hour.</i>


01:18:13.881 --> 01:18:16.577
<i>Dominating the news again here
and across the nation...</i>


01:18:16.578 --> 01:18:19.637
<i>... is the increasingly urgent search
for the Internet killer...</i>


01:18:19.638 --> 01:18:22.637
<i>... now known to be
Owen Reilly of Portland.</i>


01:18:22.797 --> 01:18:26.716
<i>His most recent victim, an FBI
cyber-crimes agent, Griffin Dowd...</i>


01:18:26.876 --> 01:18:30.311
<i>... was discovered dead in Reilly's
Fairview home basement this morning.</i>


01:18:30.679 --> 01:18:34.272
<i>In what the FBI is describing as
the most serious Internet crime wave...</i>


01:18:34.273 --> 01:18:36.713
<i>... since the computer age began...</i>


01:19:21.056 --> 01:19:22.015
Shit!


01:19:24.334 --> 01:19:25.974
<i>Hello, Jennifer.</i>


01:19:31.372 --> 01:19:33.171
<i>Look out the front window.</i>


01:19:33.931 --> 01:19:36.091
<i>Under that streetlight.</i>


01:19:37.369 --> 01:19:40.368
<i>That's where my father's body
fell over the railing.</i>


01:19:40.369 --> 01:19:43.006
<i>Some websites show the whole
thing in slow motion...</i>


01:19:43.007 --> 01:19:46.126
<i>... because it's just so much
better that way.</i>


01:19:47.846 --> 01:19:50.765
<i>One archives it in a section
called "whoa."</i>


01:19:51.445 --> 01:19:54.803
<i>That's it. Just "whoa."</i>


01:19:56.083 --> 01:19:58.122
<i>You and the people you work with...</i>


01:19:59.122 --> 01:20:02.121
<i>... you let people say and do
almost anything they want.</i>


01:20:02.281 --> 01:20:04.359
<i>It doesn't matter who it hurts.</i>


01:20:07.678 --> 01:20:09.717
I'm sorry, Owen.


01:20:13.276 --> 01:20:15.195
Owen, are you there?


01:20:48.959 --> 01:20:50.901
<i>- Call Answering Center.
- Listen.</i>


01:20:50.902 --> 01:20:52.341
I'm an agent with the FBI.


01:20:52.542 --> 01:20:55.500
I need you to connect me
to the Portland field office.


01:20:55.660 --> 01:20:56.701
Do you understand?


01:21:08.815 --> 01:21:11.175
<i>- Yeah.
- It's Owen!</i>


01:21:11.375 --> 01:21:14.013
He's hacked into my car's
computer and my cell phone.


01:21:14.173 --> 01:21:15.573
I'm on the Broadway Bridge.


01:21:15.733 --> 01:21:18.172
Don't move. I'll send a
black-and-white. Stay there.


01:21:18.532 --> 01:21:19.972
All right.


01:22:15.870 --> 01:22:17.870
<i>- Box.
- Lieutenant, I'm on the bridge.</i>


01:22:18.029 --> 01:22:19.420
<i>There's no sign of Marsh.</i>


01:22:19.549 --> 01:22:22.308
Okay. Relay that to FBI Portland.
I'm minutes away.


01:22:23.148 --> 01:22:25.365
- Hurry. Get the director on the phone.
- Yes, sir.


01:22:25.467 --> 01:22:27.826
Shut down every road to and from
the Broadway Bridge.


01:22:27.986 --> 01:22:29.906
Every car gets stopped now.


01:23:29.044 --> 01:23:32.162
I need you to run a check
on a 2006 Saab.


01:23:32.323 --> 01:23:34.841
Get me a location, start tracking.
Name: Jennifer Marsh.


01:23:35.001 --> 01:23:36.640
Portland, Oregon.


01:24:16.505 --> 01:24:19.505
Fucker disabled her car's computer.
We can't track her.


01:24:28.741 --> 01:24:30.061
Hello.


01:25:09.846 --> 01:25:11.446
You know...


01:25:11.645 --> 01:25:15.883
...l'm only doing to you
what they're going to do to me.


01:25:17.043 --> 01:25:18.602
Only...


01:25:18.882 --> 01:25:23.840
...they'll use potassium chloride, and
they won't let very many people watch.


01:25:25.240 --> 01:25:27.240
But not for long.


01:25:30.758 --> 01:25:32.077
You see, soon...


01:25:33.437 --> 01:25:38.075
...executions will be delivered
live to our TVs...


01:25:38.515 --> 01:25:43.274
...our computers, our phones,
our handhelds...


01:25:43.753 --> 01:25:46.512
...and it won't cost much.


01:25:46.672 --> 01:25:49.591
Maybe 10 bucks.


01:25:57.868 --> 01:25:59.667
Millions of eyes...


01:26:01.266 --> 01:26:04.545
...all watching the same thing
at the same time.


01:26:05.466 --> 01:26:07.864
One big, happy family.


01:26:09.704 --> 01:26:11.783
And all of it brought to you by...


01:26:17.181 --> 01:26:19.020
It doesn't matter.


01:26:22.778 --> 01:26:25.338
They'll have no trouble
finding sponsors.


01:26:55.927 --> 01:26:58.285
What's going on?
We have a signal?


01:26:58.445 --> 01:26:59.645
We're still locked out.


01:26:59.805 --> 01:27:02.084
- Stay on it.
- Yes, sir.


01:27:23.596 --> 01:27:26.755
I wonder if they'll kill you
faster or slower.


01:27:28.995 --> 01:27:31.553
Based on what I've seen online...


01:27:32.393 --> 01:27:35.871
...the awful things that men do to
women that other men pay to watch...


01:27:39.990 --> 01:27:42.389
...my guess would be faster.


01:27:46.068 --> 01:27:47.908
Much faster.


01:28:06.300 --> 01:28:08.699
Jesus Christ, it's Marsh!


01:28:21.534 --> 01:28:24.973
- This is Box.
- It's Brooks. He's got Marsh on his site.


01:28:25.933 --> 01:28:27.572
Send it to me.


01:29:44.304 --> 01:29:46.223
You're giving me my best numbers.


01:29:49.981 --> 01:29:52.941
That's... That's her basement.
He's got her in her own basement.


01:30:07.135 --> 01:30:08.495
No, no.


01:30:20.211 --> 01:30:22.370
- Did you see that?
- Fuck!


01:30:24.969 --> 01:30:26.448
Fuck!


01:30:48.000 --> 01:30:49.479
Yes!


01:31:49.480 --> 01:31:50.480
Subtitles by LeapinLar

